        rules: {
          objective: "Escape the hand. Points are awarded based on the order in which players finish. The Emperor's team wins if they finish in the top positions.",
          gameplay: "Standard climbing rules: You must play the same number of cards as the leader, but of higher rank. If someone plays four 7s, you must play four 8s or higher. If you can't or won't play, you pass.",
          keyRules: [
            'Uprising (Zaofan): Before play, Commoners can declare an uprising if they have strong hands, doubling the stakes.',
            'Tribute (Jin Gong): Losers of the previous round must give their highest cards to the winners at the start of the next round.',
            'Emperor alone: If the Emperor holds both marked cards, they play against the other four alone for quadruple points.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "As a Commoner, never trust a 'helpful' pass. If someone passes on the Emperor's 7, they might be the Eunuch saving their high cards for later.",
          intermediate: "The Lead Tactic: If you are the Emperor with many 6s (the lowest card), lead them in big sets (e.g., 'Six 6s') early. This forces the Commoners to break up their strong sets to stop you.",
          advanced: "Eunuch Camouflage: The Eunuch should intentionally play a moderately high card against the Emperor early to verify their 'loyalty' to the Commoners, then switch sides at the most damaging moment.",
          tips: [
            'Count the Jokers. There are 8 in the deck. If 6 have been played, the last 2 are the most powerful cards in existence.',
            "Don't waste 2s on small tricks. Save them to regain the lead when your team is ready to dump a long sequence of low cards.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
