          deckDescription: 'One hundred sixty-eight cards total: four standard 40-card decks (twos, threes, fours, and fives removed from each 52-card pack) combined, plus eight jokers. Four French suits in quadruplicate; red and black jokers are used as wild or special cards.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs) appear in quadruplicate (four 40-card decks). Red and black jokers are added; they may act as wild cards or have special roles in Bao Huang. Each suit has ten ranks (A, 2, 6–10, J, Q, K).',
          rankDescription: 'Ten ranks per suit in each deck: ace, two, six, seven, eight, nine, ten, jack, queen, king (threes, fours, fives removed). Eight jokers (red and black) are used; their role is defined by the game rules.',
          dealPattern: 'Single draws from wall.',
          bettingLimits: 'NA',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'Climbing combo order: single or equal-card sets; same count to beat; rank order Red Joker, Black Joker, 2, A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6.',
          rankingSystem: 'Chinese Imperial Hierarchy',
          useTrump: false,
